    "result_text": "The build succeeds and all tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned the owner identity key so duplicate detection is driven by a single SHA-256 key.\n\n**New identity key** (`OwnerIdentityKey.java`): `identityKey = SHA-256 hex over (normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName))`. It returns a 64-char lowercase hex string; `forRequest`/`forOwner` now feed `lastName` (not the old `householdId`) into the key.\n\n**New `Soundex.java`**: standard American Soundex encoder (first letter + three digits), shared by the identity key and the soft-match.\n\n**Hard duplicate (409)** (`RequireUniqueIdentity.java`): now purely a full-`identityKey` collision against existing, non-deleted owners. The separate household-duplicate 409 block (derived from `householdId`/`sharesHousehold`) is gone \u2014 two owners with the same surname and postcode but different telephones now produce different keys and are both created. The disposable email-domain blocklist still runs first, upstream in `RequireOwnerFields` (pipeline order `validate \u2192 postcode \u2192 uniqueIdentity`).\n\n**Soft match** (`AssignPossibleDuplicate.java`): now flags `possibleDuplicate` when an existing non-deleted owner has a **different** `identityKey` but the **same soundex(lastName) and postcode** (earliest/lowest-id wins). Declared household members (`sharesHousehold=true`) and owners with no postcode are still never flagged.\n\n**Kept**: `AssignHouseholdId` still assigns `householdId` \u2014 it's now used only by the household-size and membership-cap rules, not duplicate detection.\n\nDocs/comments in `AssignHouseholdId`, `DuplicateIdentityException`, and `owners.POST.yml` were updated to describe the new key. Tests: `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.",
